<title>ITALY: Flights cancelled as Italy air controllers strike.</title>
<headline>Flights cancelled as Italy air controllers strike.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian air traffic controllers staged a four-hour strike on Wednesday, causing delays to services and the cancellation of some 180 flights.</p>
<p>Further chaos was caused in Milan's Linate and Malpensa airports and at Bergamo airport in northern Italy, where ground staff also staged a 24-hour strike in protest at delays in renewal of their contracts.</p>
<p>Troubled state flag-carrier Alitalia cancelled 173 domestic flights, Air One four and Meridiana another two. Other services were delayed during the stoppage, which began at noon and was scheduled to end at four p.m. (1500 GMT).</p>
<p>Unions called the air traffic controllers' strike to demand guarantees for the future of the national flight control body.</p>
</text>
